.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH xil-cleanup 1  "xil-cleanup " 
.SH NAME
xil\-cleanup \- Remove stale stems that no longer match the current parsed script.  Use \-\-dry\-run first to review what would be deleted.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBxil\-cleanup\fR [\fB\-\-episode\fR] [\fB\-\-tag\fR] [\fB\-\-show\fR] [\fB\-\-parsed\fR] [\fB\-\-stems\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove stale stems that no longer match the current parsed script.  Use \-\-dry\-run first to review what would be deleted.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-episode\fR \fI<TAG>\fR
Episode tag (e.g. S02E03); derives \-\-parsed and \-\-stems
.TP
\fB\-\-tag\fR \fI<TAG>\fR
Raw tag for non\-episodic content (e.g. V01C03, D01); same as \-\-episode
.TP
\fB\-\-show\fR \fI<SHOW>\fR
Show name override (default: from project.json)
.TP
\fB\-\-parsed\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Parsed script JSON (overrides \-\-episode)
.TP
\fB\-\-stems\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Stems directory (overrides \-\-episode)
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
List stale stems without deleting them
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
